=== Streets ===

==== Johannesburg ====

* In 2001 The Johannesburg City Administration changed the name of DF Malan Drive to [[Beyers Naudé Drive]]. Also it changed the name of the Library Gardens to [[Beyers Naudé Square]] in order to commemorate [[Beyers Naudé]].

In 2007 the Johannesburg Development Agency changed two street names named after apartheid era ministers:<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.iol.co.za/news/politics/hendrik-verwoerd-drive-is-no-longer-357676|title=Hendrik Verwoerd Drive is no longer {{!}} IOL|website=IOL|access-date=2016-03-31}}</ref>
* [[Hendrik Verwoerd|Henrik Verwoerd]] Drive → [[Bram Fischer]] Drive
* [[Johannes Gerhardus Strijdom|Hans Strijdom]] road → [[Malibongwe Drive]]

In 2013, every street of the [[R24 (South Africa)|R24 route]] in the [[City of Johannesburg Metropolitan Municipality|Johannesburg]] and [[City of Ekurhuleni Metropolitan Municipality|Ekurhuleni]] municipalities specifically was renamed after [[Albertina Sisulu]].<ref name=":22">{{Cite journal |last=Erlank |first=Natasha |date=2017 |title=From Main Reef to Albertina Sisulu Road: The Signposted Heroine and the Politics of Memory |url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/26420986 |journal=The Public Historian |volume=39 |issue=2 |pages=31–50 |doi=10.1525/tph.2017.39.2.31 |jstor=26420986 |issn=0272-3433|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref name=":12">{{Cite web |last=Cox |first=Anna |title=Ma Sisulu's name to be on 18 Joburg streets |url=https://www.iol.co.za/news/politics/ma-sisulus-name-to-be-on-18-joburg-streets-415800 |access-date=2023-01-22 |website=www.iol.co.za |date=19 December 2002 |language=en}}</ref> Every street on this section of the R24 is now named Albertina Sisulu Road (with the exception of the westwards one-way street in Johannesburg CBD and the section between Corlett Avenue and the municipal boundary with Mogale City).<ref name=":22" /><ref name=":12" />

In 2014 the city administration continued the renaming of important streets in the city in order to "celebrate the city's shared past".<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.joburg.org.za/index.php?option=com_content&id=9175:new-street-names-celebrate-joburgs-shared-past-and-future&Itemid=266|title=city of Johannesburg - New street names celebrate Joburg's shared past … and future|last=Yollie|website=www.joburg.org.za|access-date=2016-03-31}}</ref>

